        Release(version: "2.19 (95)", date: "27 November 2026", headline: "Routes on a map, your own sleep need, gym time instead of kilograms, a gym session on any day, and the Extra workout pill moved", items: [
            "Routes · New: Progress › Routes. Before: a route showed only on the page of one done outdoor session. Now: a card ROUTES on Progress with this month's outdoor routes from Garmin on a small map, each sport in its own colour, and a line like 12 routes · 5 runs · 6 rides · 1 hike (invented). Tap it for the Routes page: a full map you can move and zoom, the month at the top with ‹ › to go back and forward, chips Run, Bike, Swim and Hike in their colours (filled = shown, outlined = hidden), and a small plate when you tap a route: the day, Garmin's name, the distance in km and the time. Done closes it; on the Mac Escape does.",
            "Routes · Good to know: what counts. Outdoor means runs, rides, open-water swims, hikes and walks with a GPS track. A treadmill run, an indoor ride, a pool swim and the gym are not on the map. Routes come from Garmin, so it needs your Garmin key on that device; without it the card says Routes come from Garmin. Add your Garmin key in Settings › Garmin. Up to 20 new routes are read on each visit, with a line like Reading 4 of 12 routes…, and each route is kept on the device, so it is read only once. Unchanged: the route on a done outdoor session's own page (since 2.8).",
            "Sleep need · New: Settings › Garmin › Sleep need. Before: Body › Sleep debt counted each night against Garmin's own sleep-need estimate, often about 8h, and the sheet said Need about 8h a night. Now: a row Sleep need right under the Garmin row, with the grey line 6h a night — your setting (or Garmin's estimate). Its page offers Garmin's estimate, 5h, 5h 30m, 6h, 6h 30m, 7h, 7h 30m, 8h, 8h 30m and 9h, with a tick beside the chosen one, and Cancel and a green Save (Escape is Cancel on the Mac). It starts at 6h, as you asked, and is the same on every device, kept in your iCloud with the app's other shared settings. With 6h set, every night counts against 6h and the sheet says Need 6h a night (your setting). Choosing Garmin's estimate brings back the old way.",
            "Body · Changed: Gym sessions show time, not kilograms. Before: the card's big figure was the kilograms lifted (like 3,250 kg), every row of the list showed kg, the line vs the one before had a kg part (+2 sets · −17 min · +640 kg), and the gym block on a strength session's page ended with the kg. Now: the big figure is the session's time (like 1h 05m); the line under it is the day and the gym, with the time not said twice; each row in the list shows the time where the kg stood; the line reads vs the one before: +4 sets · −5 min; and the gym block shows the time. The best set of each machine (best 90 kg × 10) stays as it was.",
            "Workout Companion · Changed: a gym session on a day without planned strength now shows up. Before (2.16): a finished Workout Companion session only ticked a strength session that was in the plan for that same day and still to do; on a rest day or a mobility-only day it went nowhere in this app, only to Body › Gym sessions. Now: when that day has no strength session in the plan at all, the session is added by itself as an Extra workout: Strength, its minutes, its effort 1 to 10 if Workout Companion has one, counted as training, with the note From Workout Companion. It shows wherever extras show (Today, the week strip, Sessions under Done and All, Settings › Extra workouts) and adds its time to Week so far's Strength row, but only when the plan has strength that week.",
            "Workout Companion · Good to know: the rules. Today and the 13 days before. Each Workout Companion session once only, so an extra you delete does not come back. Not when that day already has a Strength extra. A day whose planned strength session is still to do is ticked as before. A day whose planned strength is already done or marked missed gets nothing. It happens on the iPhone, where Workout Companion's notes arrive. Garmin strength activities (since 2.17) still only tick planned sessions.",
            "Today · Changed: the Extra workout pill moved. Before: the small + Extra workout pill sat at the end of the Tomorrow line, so on a day without a Tomorrow line it had a different place. Now: it sits on a line of its own directly above the Week so far card, at the right, every day. Same pill, same page.",
            "Settings · Changed: the row Thursday rides is gone from Your plan. Before: a row that offered one easy ride every Thursday, from the next Monday to your race. It had already added its rides. Now: the row is removed. The 29 rides it added (Thursday 3 December to Thursday 1 July, 30 to 60 minutes, easy) stay in the plan like any other session, and their one Undo stays in Settings › Changes to the plan. Mobility and strength is now the first row there. The rides are there because on 24 November you said yes to one easy ride a week: the bike is the longest part of a 70.3 and the plan had little easy bike time.",
            "Signs · Changed: three new signs, listed in Signs in this app. A route line in a sport's colour is the route of a session of that sport. A filled chip on the Routes page means that sport's routes are shown, an outlined one hidden. A tick beside a choice on the Sleep need page marks the chosen need. The green tick keeps its one meaning: done.",
            "Unchanged: your plan (nothing in it changes by itself; the only things added are the Extra workout for a gym session, which you can delete), Mobility and Strength ticks, the morning answer, Suggestions, Garmin's numbers, Progress's other cards, your Excel copy and iCloud. Without a Garmin key the Routes card says so, and nothing breaks.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Today (the Extra workout pill), Changing the plan (Thursday rides, Mobility and strength), Extra workouts, Body (Gym sessions, Sleep debt, Sleep need), Your two neighbour apps (a gym session on a day without strength), Progress (Routes), What this app does not do and Signs in this app.",
